1. DEFINITIONS

"End Product" means an application, website or online service that you build
with the Software and that gives its users features of its own, beyond the
Software itself. People use an End Product; they do not get the Software to
build their own software with.

"Authorized Users" means you and, if you are a company, your employees and
contractors while they work on your End Products.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Once you have paid for a license, the Licensor gives you a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, worldwide and perpetual license to:

  a) use, copy and modify the Software;

  b) use the Software to build, run and sell an unlimited number of End
     Products, for yourself or for your clients;

  c) let your Authorized Users do (a) and (b) for you.

If you build an End Product for a client, you may hand over that End Product,
including its source code, to the client. The client may use and change it only
as part of that End Product, and must follow section 3.


3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

